@startuml
title Archive Search Workbench - Network-USB\nSearch -> click -> the app attaches the right drive automatically

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam nodeFontSize 13
skinparam componentFontSize 12

actor "<b>You</b>\n<size:10>search in the browser</size>" as USER

node "<b>The machine you are working on</b>\n<size:10>recognised by your browser IP - config/remote_hosts.yaml</size>" as EXP {
  card "<b>The archived drive you want</b>\n<size:10>external USB drive / stick / SD (sticker ARCHIVE-DISK-XXX)</size>" as DISK
  component "<b>Per-machine agent</b>\n<size:10>background service: recognise (serial/UUID) + share (bind)</size>" as AGENT
  DISK --> AGENT : agent sees & shares the drive
}

cloud "<b>Your own LAN</b>\n<size:10>USB/IP over TCP 3240 (unencrypted -> LAN-only) + agent call with token</size>" as LAN

node "<b>The app host (the machine running the app)</b>\n<size:10>any host: laptop, server or NAS</size>" as SERVER {
  component "<b>Search & open</b>\n<size:10>web_app.py - Flask :5059 - result -> Open button</size>" as APP
  component "<b>Auto-attach on open</b>\n<size:10>calls the current machine's agent: bind -> attach</size>" as ORCH
  component "<b>Imports the drive over USB/IP</b>\n<size:10>usbip_ctl.sh + vhci-hcd - usbip attach</size>" as CTL
  card "<b>The drive, now visible on the host</b>\n<size:10>/dev/sdX</size>" as DEV
  component "<b>Safe open: read-only</b>\n<size:10>mount_readonly.sh - read-only + write protection</size>" as MNT
  database "<b>Catalog: what is stored where</b>\n<size:10>SQLite (searchable offline)</size>" as DB
  component "<b>Full-text searchable</b>\n<size:10>Recoll index</size>" as RECOLL

  APP --> DB : search
  APP --> ORCH : click Open on an offline file
  ORCH --> CTL : attach the drive
  CTL --> DEV
  DEV --> MNT : mount safely
  MNT --> APP : open / show file
  MNT ..> RECOLL : (when indexing)
}

USER --> APP : search + click Open
ORCH ..> AGENT : "share ARCHIVE-DISK-XXX" (via LAN, token)
AGENT --> LAN
LAN --> CTL

note right of APP
  <b>If the drive is offline: prompt + auto-detect</b>
  Shows "Connect ARCHIVE-DISK-XXX to <your machine>"
  and opens the file as soon as the agent sees the drive.
end note

note bottom of SERVER
  == Design & fallback (no silent failure) ==
  <b>Chosen:</b> a small per-machine agent -> the app handles
  detect, share, attach and open end-to-end (hands-off).
  <b>Fallback if the agent is unavailable:</b>
  1) Persistent bind: pin the drive once (admin), then auto-shared.
  2) Hybrid: agent where possible, persistent bind as safety net.
  3) Manual: Network-USB panel (usbipd bind by hand).
end note
@enduml
